.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-SSO-EXEMPT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-sso-exempt - Mark or unmark a member as SSO exempt (break-glass)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team sso exempt <team> <account> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark a member as SSO exempt so they keep access to the team without SSO, for contractors and emergency admins, or remove the mark with --remove. The owner is always exempt. Only a few members may be exempt, and every access without SSO is recorded in the audit log once a day per person.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for exempt

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--remove\fP[=false]
	remove the exemption


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-sso(1)\fP
